arm64: dts: h713: the pio has seven bank interrupts, not nine

The list was copied from the vendor DTS, which carries nine
(GIC_SPI 54..62), with the comment "Stock: GIC_SPI 54-62 for PA-PI
banks". There are no PA-PI banks on this SoC. The stock pin table
sun50iw12_pins (vmlinux.elf, c0e9d8b0, 132 pins) ends at PH19 and has
no PE and no PI pin at all, and sun50iw12_irq_bank_map (c0e9d894) is
{0, 1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7} with irq_banks = 7: seven IRQ banks, PA PB PC PD
PF PG PH. The vendor's own driver reads the first seven entries of the
list by bank index and never looks at the last two.

So the seven lines that exist are SPI 54..60, one per IRQ bank, in
irq_bank_map order -- the same shape upstream uses for the H616, which
has the same gap and lists seven consecutive lines for it. SPI 61 and
62 belong to nothing here, and leaving them in invites exactly the
mistake patch 0143 undoes: reading the list as if it were indexed by
hardware bank number, which puts the chained handler of one bank on
another bank's line and live-locks the CPU on the first edge.

This patch is documentation, not the fix. 0143 alone makes the device
boot; with 0143 applied the first seven entries are the ones used
either way. Applying this one *without* 0143 does not help -- the
hw_bank lookup would then ask for index 7, get -ENXIO and silently
switch off GPIO interrupts on the whole main PIO. Apply 0143 first.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -493,16 +493,23 @@
 			#gpio-cells = <3>;
 			interrupt-controller;
 			#interrupt-cells = <3>;
-			/* Stock: GIC_SPI 54-62 for PA-PI banks */
-			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 54 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
-				     <GIC_SPI 55 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
-				     <GIC_SPI 56 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
-				     <GIC_SPI 57 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
-				     <GIC_SPI 58 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
-				     <GIC_SPI 59 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
-				     <GIC_SPI 60 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
-				     <GIC_SPI 61 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
-				     <GIC_SPI 62 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			/*
+			 * One line per IRQ bank, in irq_bank_map order, not
+			 * one per hardware bank: PA PB PC PD PF PG PH.
+			 * PE has no pins and no EINT block on this SoC
+			 * (sun50iw12_pins / sun50iw12_irq_bank_map in the
+			 * stock vmlinux), so there is no line for it and the
+			 * numbers do not skip. The vendor DTS lists nine
+			 * (SPI 54..62) and its driver reads only the first
+			 * seven -- the last two belong to nothing here.
+			 */
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 54 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,	/* PA */
+				     <GIC_SPI 55 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,	/* PB */
+				     <GIC_SPI 56 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,	/* PC */
+				     <GIC_SPI 57 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,	/* PD */
+				     <GIC_SPI 58 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,	/* PF */
+				     <GIC_SPI 59 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,	/* PG */
+				     <GIC_SPI 60 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;	/* PH */
 
 			mmc2_pins: mmc2-pins {
 				pins = "PC0", "PC1", "PC5", "PC6",
